# Dashboard Storybook routing

`apps/dashboard/.storybook/preview.tsx` wraps **every** story in `MemoryRouter`.

- **Do not** import or render `MemoryRouter`, `BrowserRouter`, `RouterProvider`,
  `createBrowserRouter`, or `createMemoryRouter` in `*.stories.tsx` decorators.
- Nested routers cause runtime errors (`You cannot render a <Router> inside another <Router>`)
  and fail the Storybook test runner.
- **Vitest** (`*.test.tsx`) has no global router — wrap there only when the component
  uses `Link`, `NavLink`, `useNavigate`, `useParams`, etc.
- If the component uses plain `#` anchors or props only, skip routers in both stories and tests.
- For layout-only decorators, wrap with `<div>` / page shells — not a router.
- To simulate a URL in a story, extend preview or use story `parameters` — never nest routers.

See [apps/dashboard/docs/feature-conventions.md](../../apps/dashboard/docs/feature-conventions.md#storybook).
